  "generated_text": "To find the length of the paint trail left by the tennis ball, we need to compute the arc length of the curve given by the parametric equations:\n\\[\nx(t) = 3t^2 - 9t - 5\n\\]\n\\[\ny(t) = t^2 - 3t + 2\n\\]\nfor \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\).\n\nThe formula for the arc length \\(L\\) of a parametric curve \\((x(t), y(t))\\) from \\(t = a\\) to \\(t = b\\) is:\n\\[\nL = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to find \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\) and \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\).\n\n1. Compute \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\):\n\\[\nx(t) = 3t^2 - 9t - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(3t^2 - 9t - 5) = 6t - 9\n\\]\n\n2. Compute \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\):\n\\[\ny(t) = t^2 - 3t + 2\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(t^2 - 3t + 2) = 2t - 3\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\) and \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\) into the arc length formula:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{\\left(6t - 9\\right)^2 + \\left(2t - 3\\right)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n\\[\n\\left(6t - 9\\right)^2 = (6t - 9)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left(2t - 3\\right)^2 = (2t - 3)^2 = 4t^2 - 12t + 9\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left(6t - 9\\right)^2 + \\left(2t - 3\\right)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81 + 4t^2 - 12t + 9 = 40t^2 - 120t + 90\n\\]\n\n4. Factor out the common term:\n\\[\n40t^2 - 120t + 90 = 10(4t^2 - 12t + 9)\n\\]\n\\[\n4t^2 - 12t + 9 = (2t - 3)^2\n\\]\n\\[\n10(4t^2 - 12t + 9) = 10(2t - 3)^2\n\\]\n\n5. Take the square root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{10(2t - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{10} \\cdot |2t - 3|\n\\]\n\nSince \\(2t - 3\\) can be positive or negative depending on the value of \\(t\\), we need to consider the absolute value. However, for \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\), \\(2t - 3\\) ranges from \\(-3\\) to \\(5\\), so \\(|2t - 3| = 2t - 3\\) when \\(2t - 3 \\ge 0\\) and \\(|2t - 3| = -(2t - 3)\\) when \\(2t - 3 < 0\\). But since \\(2t - 3\\) is non-negative in the interval \\([0, 4]\\), we have:\n\\[\n|2t - 3| = 2t - 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the integrand simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{10} \\cdot (2t - 3)\n\\]\n\n6. Set up and evaluate the integral:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{10} \\cdot (2t - 3) \\, dt\n\\]\n\\[\nL = \\sqrt{10} \\int_0^4 (2t - 3) \\, dt\n\\]\n\n7. Compute the integral:\n\\[\n\\int_0^4 (2t - 3) \\, dt = \\left[ t^2 - 3t \\right]_0^4\n\\]\n\\[\n= (4^2 - 3 \\cdot 4) - (0^2 - 3 \\cdot 0)\n\\]\n\\[\n= (16 - 12) - 0\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4\n\\]\n\n8. Multiply by \\(\\sqrt{10}\\):\n\\[\nL = \\sqrt{10} \\cdot 4 = 4\\sqrt{10}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the paint trail left by the tennis ball is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4\\sqrt{10}}\n\\]",
